>> title: Date Squares
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: dates, oats, dessert, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: date bars, matrimonial cake, date crumble squares
>> servings: 9
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.5: layer crumble, filling, crumble

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C).

Line an #8x8-in pan{} with parchment.

Simmer @chopped pitted dates{2%cup}(340 g), @water{3/4%cup}(180 mL), @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #saucepan{} for ~{10%min}, until jammy.

Rub @cold unsalted butter{3/4%cup}(170 g) into @rolled oats{1 1/2%cup}(135 g), @all-purpose flour{1 1/4%cup}(160 g), @light brown sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g), @baking soda{1/2%tsp}(2.5 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Press half of @&(~1)oat crumble{} into the pan, spread @&(~2)date filling{} over it, and scatter the rest of the crumble on top.

Bake @&(~1)squares{} at 350°F for ~{35%min}.
